sequenceDiagram
    participant B as Blocker
    participant R as Ordinary reader
    participant W as Waiter
    participant O as Observer

    B->>B: BEGIN; UPDATE order 1002
    Note over B: New tuple version is uncommitted
    R->>B: plain SELECT
    B-->>R: does not block; old committed version is visible
    W->>B: UPDATE the same row
    Note over W: waits on Blocker's transaction ID
    O->>O: pg_stat_activity + pg_blocking_pids + pg_locks
    O->>B: pg_cancel_backend(exact PID)
    Note over B: connection exits; transaction rolls back
    B-->>W: conflicting lock is released
    W->>W: UPDATE succeeds, then ROLLBACK
    O->>O: verify original fingerprint and no workers
